  partName: Right Front Sensor (2)
  description: The Right Front Sensor (2) is a tiny, elongated sensor located at
    the middle-right-front of the engine, serving a similar purpose to its left-front
    counterpart by monitoring engine parameters and providing data to the control
    unit. Its tiny size and elongated shape enable it to be mounted in a compact
    space, allowing for efficient data collection. Interestingly, the sensor's material
    composition, Material.001, provides excellent durability and resistance to extreme
    temperatures.
